ancellationToken)","fullName":"BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.BlobBytesStorageExtensions.DownloadBytesManyAsync(BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.IBlobStoreClient, System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable, BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.BlobBytesDownloadManyOptions, System.Threading.CancellationToken)","kind":"Method","namespace":"BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage","assembly":"BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage","summary":"Downloads many blobs into byte arrays using bounded parallelism. When the provider supports batched downloads (Entity Framework), the keys are read with a few multi-key queries instead of one query per key. Every key still passes through the complete client behavior pipeline individually. All downloaded content is buffered in memory, so use it for many small blobs only.","remarks":null,"syntax":{"content":"public static Task\u003E\u003E DownloadBytesManyAsync(this IBlobStoreClient blobClient, IEnumerable blobKeys, BlobBytesDownloadManyOptions options = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)","parameters":[{"id":"blobClient","type":"BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.IBlobStoreClient","description":"The blob client to download from."},{"id":"blobKeys","type":"System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable{BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.BlobKey}","description":"The keys to download. A duplicate key is read once per occurrence, but only its first occurrence is batched."},{"id":"options","type":"BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.BlobBytesDownloadManyOptions","description":"Optional bulk download options."},{"id":"cancellationToken","type":"System.Threading.CancellationToken","description":"A token to cancel the downloads."}],"returns":{"type":"System.Threading.Tasks.Task{BridgingIT.DevKit.Common.Result{System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList{BridgingIT.DevKit.Application.Storage.BlobBytesDownloadManyItem}}}","description":"A result containing one item per requested key in the order of blobKeys. With Bridging